{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 840 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Fludarabine phosphate has been on FDA's shortage list since 2022-05-06 and remains listed as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at Corvale General and Corvale East carries NDC 45963060955 and is labeled by Actavis Pharma, Inc.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That label names ACTAVIS TOTOWA as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1142104 at the associated facility (FEI 3004762406, NerPharMa S.r.l.) ended 2020-01-17 and was classified VAI, with the classification letter dated 2021-05-19 — 840 days before FDA posted the shortage on 2022-05-06.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No FDA inspection at a registered plant for this product occurred after the shortage posting, so the record shows a VAI classification well before the posting but no later action tied to the shortage.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E10", "E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑based best option is to transfer 18 vials of 50 mg/2 mL, 2 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East; Corvale General has 18.2 days on hand and can spare the vials while keeping two weeks, and Corvale East would rise from 4.4 days to about 10 days.",
      "cites": ["D3", "D4", "D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Alternate manufacturers Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC (plant last inspected VAI 2023-08-24) and Hisun Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. (no plant identified on label) are not on FDA's shortage list today.",
      "cites": ["D9", "D10"]
    }
  ]
}
